  <h2>How this changes Kakobuy Spreadsheet planning</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/blog/mixing-categories-outbound-parcel-spreadsheet-2026/">mixed-category parcel guide</a> already explains why shoes, perfume, and electronics can complicate routing.
    The July 2026 EU duty update adds another reason to think before combining everything into one box.
    Buyers should log category, approximate customs value, and intended destination before rehearsal packaging.
    If the haul is EU-bound, the savings from consolidation should be compared against the new per-item duty environment and the courier’s handling behaviour.
  </p>

  <h2>What not to do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Do not invent false descriptions.</strong> Vague or inaccurate descriptions can trigger holds under newer data systems.</li>
    <li><strong>Do not assume IOSS solves everything.</strong> VAT handling and the new temporary duty are separate issues in the EU guidance.</li>
    <li><strong>Do not split parcels blindly.</strong> Splitting can reduce category complexity but may increase freight, handling, or delivery fees.</li>
    <li><strong>Do not copy another buyer’s declaration.</strong> Their country, line, and item mix may not match your haul.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>EU buyers should update their checklist</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Start from a clear category path such as <a href="/category/shoes/">Shoes</a>, <a href="/category/t-shirts/">T-shirts</a>, or <a href="/category/accessories/">Accessories</a>.</li>
    <li>Before international shipping, list each product type in the parcel.</li>
    <li>Read the broader <a href="/blog/eu-import-vat-landed-cost-spreadsheet-buyers/">EU VAT and landed-cost guide</a>.</li>
    <li>Use <a href="/blog/kakobuy-freight-line-picker-spreadsheet-2026/">freight line selection</a> to compare routing, not just headline price.</li>
    <li>Keep screenshots and order notes in case a courier asks for clarification.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Bottom line</h2>
  <p>
    The July 2026 EU change makes item-level customs data more important for spreadsheet buyers.
    Kakobuy users do not need to panic, but EU-bound hauls should stop treating customs as a single afterthought at the end of checkout.
    Build the duty estimate while the cart is still flexible.
  </p>
